course: dictionary
lesson: 15583
title: Symbiotic: living together and helping each other
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some living things depend on each other so much that they live together for a long time. A close, helpful partnership like this is called symbiotic. The start of the word, sym-, means together, and biotic is about living things.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Bees visit the flowers to drink nectar, and the flowers get their pollen carried to other flowers.» Both sides gain from this. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A close, helpful partnership fits.
explain: The word is not only for animals and plants. «The farm and the village had a symbiotic relationship: the farm sold food, and the village sold tools.» Here symbiotic describes people helping each other. Try swapping in the simple meaning, "helpful partnership", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Symbiotic describes a close relationship between two different living things that live together.
fact: «Symbiotic» can also describe people, groups or things that help each other.
fact: Lichen is a fungus and an alga living together, and both partners get help from each other.
fact: In some relationships one partner gains and the other is not harmed, while in others one gains and the other is harmed.
fact: The bacteria in our gut are symbiotic: they help us digest food, and we give them a home.
exercise: «Clownfish live safely among the stinging tentacles of a sea anemone, and the anemone is protected too.» What does symbiotic describe here? | A fish that is hunted by sharks | A plant that grows alone in the sea | *A close relationship where both living things are helped | A sudden storm on the coast
exercise: Which is a symbiotic relationship? | A tree growing alone on a hill | A cat hunting a mouse in a field | A rock sitting on the beach | *Bees and flowers, where the bees get nectar and the flowers get pollen moved
exercise: The word «symbiotic» starts with the prefix sym-. What does sym- mean? | *Together | Apart | Underground | Very big
test: «The farm and the village had a symbiotic relationship.» Which is the best meaning? | A shop that sells only bread | *A helpful partnership where both sides gain | A quarrel that never ends | A long journey by train
test: Lichens are symbiotic because a fungus and an alga live together. What do both partners get? | Only the fungus gains | Harm from each other | Nothing at all | *Help from each other
exam: Which word describes the bacteria in our gut, which help us and are helped by us? | *Symbiotic | Famished | Luminous | Treacherous
